	(text "Five MP8759 converters, each copied from the 5 V stage of the Radxa Rock 5B v1.45 schematic, sheet 20.\nDifferences from the reference, to be checked against the MP8759 datasheet before layout:\n  - all five run directly from VIN (the reference feeds its 4 V stage from the 5 V rail);\n  - the three 3.3 V rails are new, with a 47K / 10.2K divider (0.6 V reference gives 3.36 V);\n  - every stage uses 1.5 uH, the datasheet's table value for 3.3 V and 5 V outputs;\n  - ENABLE: the pin's absolute maximum is 4.5 V. The 5 V and 4 V stages start with VIN through a\n    100K / 75K divider clamped by a 3.6 V zener. The three 3.3 V stages are switched by logic:\n    +3V3 and VCC_3V3_M2 follow VCC_3V3_S0, so nothing feeds the processor's pins before its own\n    supplies are up; VCC_MODEM is switched by software so a hung modem can be power-cycled.\n26 V is the MP8759's ABSOLUTE MAXIMUM input, not a working limit: power the board from 20 V or less\n(USB-C PD up to 20 V, or a 12 V to 19 V DC supply). The power entry sheet feeds VIN."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15 15 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "9ef5fc55-5b07-5176-8442-922fce843ee8")
	)
	(text "5.05 V: USB ports (5.25 V is the limit with tolerances). On whenever VIN is present"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
